1	73	\N	\N	A company is producing a new product, and the cost of producing x units is given by the polynomial C(x) = 2x^2 + 5x + 3. If the company wants to break even, it needs to produce at least 2 units. What can be concluded about the graph of C(x) and the solutions to the equation C(x) = 0?			mcq	understand	medium	1	90	Since the company needs to produce at least 2 units to break even, the cost function C(x) must be equal to 0 when x = 2. This means that the graph of C(x) has at least one x-intercept at x = 2, and the solution to C(x) = 0 is x = 2.			\N	\N	\N	ai	APPROVED	\N	\N	f	72	2026-07-06 05:12:34.786549	2026-07-06 05:12:34.786558
1	73	\N	\N	A company is planning to manufacture and sell a new product. The cost of producing x units of the product is given by the polynomial 2x^2 + 5x + 3. The revenue from selling x units of the product is given by the polynomial 4x^2 - 2x + 1. If the profit is represented by the polynomial P(x), what is the value of x for which the profit is maximum?			mcq	understand	medium	1	120	To find the value of x for which the profit is maximum, we need to find the x-intercepts of the profit polynomial P(x) = (4x^2 - 2x + 1) - (2x^2 + 5x + 3) = 2x^2 - 7x - 2. The x-intercepts of this polynomial are the values of x for which the profit is zero. We can find the x-intercepts by factoring the polynomial or by using the quadratic formula. The quadratic formula gives us x = (-b ± √(b^2 - 4ac)) / 2a, where a = 2, b = -7, and c = -2. Plugging in these values, we get x = (7 ± √((-7)^2 - 4(2)(-2))) / (2(2)) = (7 ± √(49 + 16)) / 4 = (7 ± √65) / 4. Since the profit is maximum at one of the x-intercepts, we need to find the value of x that is closer to the vertex of the parabola. The vertex of the parabola is given by x = -b / 2a = -(-7) / (2(2)) = 7/4. The value of x that is closer to the vertex is x = (7 - √65) / 4.			\N	\N	\N	ai	APPROVED	\N	\N	f	73	2026-07-06 05:12:34.799601	2026-07-06 05:12:34.799609
1	87	\N	\N	A company is planning to manufacture a new product. The cost of producing x units of the product is given by the equation 2x^2 + 5x - 3 = 0. If the company wants to produce 15 units of the product, will it incur a loss or profit?			mcq	understand	medium	1	90	To determine whether the company will incur a loss or profit, we need to find the value of the cost function at x = 15. We can do this by substituting x = 15 into the equation 2x^2 + 5x - 3 = 0. If the result is positive, the company will incur a profit. If the result is negative, the company will incur a loss.			\N	\N	\N	ai	APPROVED	\N	\N	f	74	2026-07-06 05:12:43.377672	2026-07-06 05:12:43.377681
1	87	\N	\N	A company is planning to manufacture a new product. The cost of producing x units of the product is given by the equation 2x^2 + 5x - 3 = 0. If the company wants to produce 15 units of the product, will they incur a profit or a loss?			mcq	understand	medium	1	90	To determine whether the company will incur a profit or a loss, we need to find the value of the cost function at x = 15. We can do this by substituting x = 15 into the equation 2x^2 + 5x - 3 = 0. If the result is positive, the company will incur a loss. If the result is negative, the company will incur a profit.			\N	\N	\N	ai	APPROVED	\N	\N	f	75	2026-07-06 05:12:43.381072	2026-07-06 05:12:43.381078
